---
chartdown: 0.9
title: Syntax Tour
key: D
tempo: 90
meter: 4/4
feel: Straight
instruments: cello
---

// Every feature of ChartDown 0.9, one section each.
// Each section name starts with its section number in SPEC.md.
// Lines that start with // are comments and are not shown.

## 4 · Notes for each player
> A plain note, for everyone.
> MD: An MD note for the whole band.
> MD drums, bass: Lock in together. Try the View menu to read just your part.
> MD keys, gtr, vox: One note for several players.
> MD sax, tpt, tbn, vln: Horn and string roles.
> MD cello: A custom instrument, declared in the header.
1 | 4 | 5 | 1

## 5 · Bars and rows
> Bars are separated by |. Each line is one row. Numbers or letters.
1 | 4 | 5 | 1
D | G | A | D

## 5.1 · Splitting a bar
> Chords share a bar evenly. Use :beats for uneven splits.
1 4 | 6m 5 | 1:3 4:1 | 5:2 4 5

## 5.2 · Reusing a section
> MD: This section copies the rows of "5 · Bars and rows" with @use, and plays them twice.
@use 5 · Bars and rows 2x

## 5.3 · Pickup bar
> MD gtr: Pickup on beat 3. A pickup is bar 0 and is drawn narrower.
[p:2] 5 | 1 | 4 | 5 | 1

## 6 · Chords
> Major, minor, sevenths, suspended, other qualities, slash chords, outside the key.
> Aliases take their canonical form: M7 is maj7, ø is m7b5, + is aug.
1 | 6m 6- | 5sus 5 | 1maj7 4add9
2m7 5/7 | 1/3 4 | b7 #4dim | Em C/E
4M7 7ø | 37b9 6m | 5+ 4(add9) | 15 b75

## 7 · Rests and repeat signs
> x is no chord. x:3 rests three beats. % repeats the bar. = ties the chord over.
x | 1! x:3 | 4 | % | <1> | =

## 7.1 · Unison riff
> MD gtr, tpt: Unison line in single notes. Notes take :beats, x is a rest.
1 | R[ 1 3 4 #4 5 ] | 4 | R[ 5:1 b7:1 x:2 ]

## 8 · Expression marks
> ' pushes an eighth early, '' a sixteenth. <1> holds, ! stabs, ~ is a fermata.
'4 | ''5 | <1> | 4! 5! | <1>~

## 9 · Dynamics, cues and lyric landmarks
> Dynamics: pp p mp mf f ff cresc decresc. Cues for everyone or one player.
{pp} 1 | {p} 4 | {mp} 5 | {mf} 1
{f} 4 {watch me} | {ff} 5 {drums: fill} | {cresc} 1 "Short words, where we are" | {decresc} 1

## 9 · Tempo marks
> rit. slows down, accel. speeds up, a tempo goes back.
4 | 5 {rit} | {a tempo} 1 | {accel} 1

## 9.1 · Cues for one pass
> MD 2x keys: Pad comes in on the second pass.
|: 1 {2x drums: in} | 4 | 5 {1x,3x: stop} | 1 :| 3x

## 10 · Repeats and endings
> |: and :| repeat, 2x or 3x counts the passes. [1] and [2] are endings.
|: 1 | 4 | 1 | [1] 5 :| 2x
[2] 5 4 5 1 |

## 11.1 · Key changes
> MD: Up a whole step, then a minor key. In a minor key 1m is the tonic.
@key E
1 | 4 | 5 | 1
@key Bm
1m | b6 | b3 | b7

## 11.2 · Meter changes
> @meter changes the meter from here on. [m:2/4] changes one bar.
@key D
@meter 3/4
1 | 4 | 5 | 1
@meter 4/4
4 | [m:2/4] 5 | 1 | 1

## 11.3 · Tempo changes
> @tempo changes the tempo from here on; q. says one beat is a dotted quarter.
@tempo 72
{p} 6m | 4 | 1 | 5
@meter 6/8
@tempo 48 q.
1 | 4 | 5 | 1
@meter 4/4

## 10.1 · Navigation: segno
> MD: The D.S. below jumps back here. "To coda" only counts after the jump.
@tempo 90
{segno} 1 | 4 | 5 {to coda} | 5

## 10.1 · Navigation: D.S. al Coda
> MD: Also {D.C.}, {fine}, {D.S. al fine}, {D.C. al coda}. One jump per song.
6m | 4 | 1 | 5 {D.S. al coda}

## 10.1 · Navigation: coda
{coda} {f} 4 | 5 | <1>~
